    "question": {
      ":question/id": "0173f834-c4db-5b67-b279-f8f88dbe9092",
      ":question/problem": "Solve the following system of equations:\n    \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=8 \\\\ {x}_{2}-6{x}_{3} &=12 \\\\ {x}_{3} &=- \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "The third equation states that ${x}_{3}=- \\frac{4}{3}.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6(- \\frac{4}{3})=12\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{2}=12-(8)=4.\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute ${x}_{2}=4$ and ${x}_{3}=- \\frac{4}{3}$ into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+(4)-(- \\frac{4}{3})=8\\,\u27f9\\,{x}_{1}=8-(4)-(\\frac{4}{3})=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is ${x}_{1}=\\frac{8}{3}$, ${x}_{2}=4$, and ${x}_{3}=- \\frac{4}{3}.$ In vector form, the solution can be written as $\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{3} \\\\ 4 \\\\ - \\frac{4}{3}\\end{bmatrix}.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
